{"id":3995171977012,"type":"album","name":"Something/Anything?","artist":"Todd Rundgren","year":1972,"weight":25,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710804.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-6e06aa09-3298-4d4f-a37d-ccae5c14a0a2/mbid-6e06aa09-3298-4d4f-a37d-ccae5c14a0a2-41471726611.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":13,"country":"GB","yt":"N5V5HktI4Kg","desc":"Something/Anything? is the third album by American musician Todd Rundgren, released in February 1972. It was Rundgren's first album released under his own name, following two records credited to the quasi-group project Runt, and was also his first double album. It was recorded in late 1971 in Los Angeles, New York City and Bearsville Studios, Woodstock. The album is divided into four sections focused on different stylistic themes; the first three parts were recorded in the studio with Rundgren playing all instruments and singing all vocals in addition to producing. The final quarter contained a number of tracks recorded live .","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/todd-rundgren/something-anything"}},"artist_ref":{"id":155463229665045,"name":"Todd Rundgren","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/ToddRundgren.png?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":185670346256268,"type":"genre","name":"rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":3782,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":30277598324326,"type":"genre","name":"pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1523,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":18872195504512,"type":"genre","name":"Pop Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":740,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":191826593279813,"type":"genre","name":"Art Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":531,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":138197775829889,"type":"genre","name":"Progressive Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":439,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":121661734395550,"type":"genre","name":"Power Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":369,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":126